from tnx import *
def T(iy,iyn,*a): TA(9,iy,iyn,*a)
I3="Iyal 3: Culture and Humanity (பண்பாடு, மனிதம்)"
T(3,I3,"yeru-thazhuvuthal","Yeru Thazhuvuthal (ஏறு தழுவுதல்) — bull taming",
 "For the Tamils, bulls stand for courage, harvest and wealth.",
 "Yeru Thazhuvuthal, the embracing of the bull, is an ancient sport of the Mullai and Marutham regions that became part of Tamil culture. The prose lesson explains that cattle are symbols of bravery, harvest, prosperity and wealth for Tamils.",
 "The sport shows the courage of young men and the closeness between farmers and their cattle. It is described in Sangam literature and is a part of Tamil heritage.",
 "Terms: ஏறு (bull), தழுவுதல் (to embrace), முல்லை and மருதம் (landscapes), பண்பாடு (culture) and வீரம் (bravery).",
 ["ஏறு","தழுவுதல்","முல்லை","மருதம்","பண்பாடு"],
 ("Yeru thazhuvuthal is a game of cards.",["It is a bull-taming sport.","It is ancient Tamil culture."]),
 ["m|ஏறு means|bull|horse|bird|Bull.","m|The sport is associated with|Mullai and Marutham lands|sea coast|snow lands|The pastoral and farming regions.","t|It shows the bravery of young men.|T|Yes.","m|Cattle stand for|wealth and bravery|sadness|travel|Tamil symbols.","s|What does பண்பாடு mean?|culture|Culture.","t|It is part of Tamil heritage.|T|Yes."])
T(3,I3,"manimegalai","Manimegalai (மணிமேகலை)",
 "A great Tamil epic where compassion feeds the hungry.",
 "Manimegalai is one of the five great Tamil epics (ஐம்பெருங்காப்பியங்கள்), composed by Seethalai Saathanaar. It is the story of Manimegalai, the daughter of Kovalan and Madhavi, who leaves her dancing family's life and becomes a Buddhist nun.",
 "The epic is known for its message of charity and service. Manimegalai receives the Amuthasurabi, an inexhaustible bowl that always gives food, and she uses it to feed the hungry.",
 "Learn the terms காப்பியம் (epic), பெருங்காப்பியம், அமுதசுரபி (the bowl of plenty) and பசிப்பிணி (the disease of hunger). It is a memorisation poem in the book.",
 ["காப்பியம்","மணிமேகலை","அமுதசுரபி","சீத்தலைச் சாத்தனார்","பசிப்பிணி"],
 ("Manimegalai is a story of war.",["It is a story of service.","Her bowl feeds the hungry."]),
 ["m|Manimegalai was composed by|Seethalai Saathanaar|Ilango|Kamban|Seethalai Saathanaar.","m|Her magic bowl is the|Amuthasurabi|Kamandalam|Chakra|Amuthasurabi.","t|Manimegalai is one of the five great epics.|T|Yes.","m|The epic teaches|charity|hatred|trade|Feeding the hungry.","s|Whose daughter is Manimegalai?|Kovalan and Madhavi;Kovalan|Daughter of Kovalan and Madhavi.","t|Manimegalai became a Buddhist nun.|T|Yes."])
T(3,I3,"margazhip-peruvizha","Margazhip Peruvizha (மார்கழிப் பெருவிழா)",
 "Waking before dawn in the cold month of Margazhi has been a Tamil tradition for ages.",
 "This lesson says that our ancestors lived in harmony with nature and divided life into landscapes (திணை). They rose early, worshipped God and began their day with prayer. In the month of Margazhi they observed vows (நோன்பு) and sang to God.",
 "The festival shows how Tamil culture links nature, devotion and community. Songs like Thiruppavai and Thiruvempavai are sung in this month.",
 "Terms: மார்கழி (the Tamil month Dec-Jan), நோன்பு (vow), இறைவழிபாடு (worship) and பண்பாடு (culture).",
 ["மார்கழி","நோன்பு","இறைவழிபாடு","திணை","பண்பாடு"],
 ("Margazhi is a summer festival.",["It is in the cold month.","Prayer starts before dawn."]),
 ["m|Margazhi is a|Tamil month|day|year|Dec-Jan.","m|People in this month observe|vows (nonbu)|a sports meet|an exam|Nonbu.","t|Ancestors lived close to nature.|T|Yes.","m|The day begins with|early rising and prayer|late sleep|travel|Tradition.","s|What do we call a vow in Tamil?|நோன்பு;nonbu|நோன்பு.","t|Songs are sung in Margazhi.|T|Yes."])
T(3,I3,"thaimaikku-varatchi-illai","Thaimaikku Varatchi Illai (தாய்மைக்கு வறட்சி இல்லை!)",
 "Even in drought, a mother's love never dries up.",
 "This short story by S. Samuthiram shows humanity (மனிதம்) through motherhood. All kinds of literature speak about humanity, and Tamil short stories do too. The story says that whatever may dry up, human kindness must not.",
 "Through the story, motherhood becomes the way in which humanity is protected. It teaches that love and care for others do not depend on wealth.",
 "Terms: தாய்மை (motherhood), வறட்சி (drought), மனிதம் (humanity) and சிறுகதை (short story).",
 ["தாய்மை","வறட்சி","மனிதம்","சிறுகதை","பண்பாடு"],
 ("The story is about a farmer's loss only.",["It is about motherhood and humanity.","Love never dries up."]),
 ["m|The story is by|S. Samuthiram|Kandharvan|Kannadasan|S. Samuthiram.","m|The title means motherhood has no|drought|joy|food|வறட்சி is drought.","t|Humanity is the theme.|T|Yes.","m|சிறுகதை is a|short story|poem|play|Short story.","s|தாய்மை means|motherhood|Motherhood.","t|The story says kindness must not dry up.|T|Yes."])
T(3,I3,"thodar-ilakkanam-aaguperayar","Grammar: Sentence structure and Aaguperayar (தொடர் இலக்கணம், ஆகுபெயர்)",
 "Sometimes a name is used for something connected to it.",
 "ஆகுபெயர் is a word that, instead of meaning its own thing, denotes something closely related to it. For example, when we say 'the whole village came', ஊர் stands for the people of the village.",
 "The main kinds are பொருளாகுபெயர், இடவாகுபெயர், காலவாகுபெயர், சினையாகுபெயர், பண்பாகுபெயர் and தொழிலாகுபெயர். The textbook also teaches how words join to make a sentence (தொடர்).",
 "Practise identifying which type it is: a place name for its people is இடவாகுபெயர்; a time name for what happens in it is காலவாகுபெயர்; a part for the whole is சினையாகுபெயர்.",
 ["ஆகுபெயர்","தொடர்","இடவாகுபெயர்","காலவாகுபெயர்","சினையாகுபெயர்"],
 ("Aaguperayar always names the same thing.",["It names a related thing.","Example: ஊர் for the people."]),
 ["m|Aaguperayar means|a name used for a related thing|a verb|a pronoun|By definition.","m|Place for its people is|இடவாகுபெயர்|காலவாகுபெயர்|பண்பாகுபெயர்|Idavaguperayar.","t|Aaguperayar has six types.|T|Yes.","m|Part for the whole is|சினையாகுபெயர்|காலவாகுபெயர்|தொழிலாகுபெயர்|Sinai means part.","s|What is a sentence called in Tamil grammar here?|தொடர்;thodar|தொடர்.","t|The village that came stands for the people.|T|Yes."])
T(3,I3,"thirukkural-iyal3","Thirukkural (திருக்குறள்) — selected couplets, Iyal 3",
 "Thiruvalluvar says a great deal in two short lines.",
 "Thirukkural, by Thiruvalluvar, is a universal book of ethics with 1330 couplets (குறள்) in 133 chapters, divided into three parts: அறம் (virtue), பொருள் (wealth) and இன்பம் (love). The textbook gives selected couplets for this unit.",
 "Each kural has seven words in two lines, a short form called kural venba. The couplets teach conduct and humanity. For this unit the selection links to culture and human values.",
 "For each kural learn the meaning of every word, the central message and the chapter heading. Learn the terms குறள் வெண்பா, அதிகாரம் (chapter) and அறம்.",
 ["குறள்","அதிகாரம்","அறம்","பொருள்","இன்பம்"],
 ("Thirukkural has 1000 couplets.",["It has 1330.","It has 133 chapters."]),
 ["m|Thirukkural has how many couplets?|1330|1000|133|1330 kurals.","m|It was written by|Thiruvalluvar|Kamban|Ilango|Valluvar.","t|It has three parts: aram, porul, inbam.|T|Yes.","m|Each chapter is called an|athikaram|kaandam|padalam|Chapter.","s|How many chapters does Thirukkural have?|133;133 chapters|133.","t|A kural has two lines.|T|Yes."])
I4="Iyal 4: Education (கல்வி)"
T(4,I4,"kalviyil-sirandha-pengal","Kalviyil Sirandha Pengal (கல்வியில் சிறந்த பெண்கள்)",
 "Knowledge lasts longer than any treasure in our hands.",
 "This prose lesson says that education stays with a person for life and is more lasting than wealth. Women's education was high in the Sangam period, declined in the middle ages and was brought back through the efforts of reformers across the world.",
 "It honours women who excelled in learning. The lesson teaches that girls' education is important for the family and the nation.",
 "Terms: கல்வி (education), பெண்கல்வி (women's education), சங்ககாலம் (Sangam age) and சான்றோர் (the wise).",
 ["கல்வி","பெண்கல்வி","சங்ககாலம்","சான்றோர்","மறுமலர்ச்சி"],
 ("Women's education was never important.",["It was high in Sangam times.","It was revived later."]),
 ["m|Education is more lasting than|wealth|breath|time|Knowledge stays for life.","m|Women's education was high in|the Sangam age|the middle ages|modern times only|Sangam period.","t|Education is a lasting wealth.|T|Yes.","m|பெண்கல்வி is|women's education|a poem|a festival|Women's education.","s|What is கல்வி in English?|education|Education.","t|Reformers worked for women's education.|T|Yes."])
T(4,I4,"kudumba-vilakku","Kudumba Vilakku (குடும்ப விளக்கு) by Bharathidasan",
 "A poet shows a woman as the lamp of her family.",
 "Kudumba Vilakku is a work of Bharathidasan, a poet of the twentieth-century renaissance (மறுமலர்ச்சி இலக்கியம்). Such literature praised nature, aroused Tamil feeling, spread rational thought, spoke of equality, urged freedom and stressed women's education.",
 "The poem presents the household woman as the lamp that gives light to her family, and it values learning and good character.",
 "Terms: குடும்ப விளக்கு (family lamp), மறுமலர்ச்சி (renaissance), பகுத்தறிவு (rationalism) and பாரதிதாசன்.",
 ["மறுமலர்ச்சி","பகுத்தறிவு","குடும்பம்","பாரதிதாசன்","விளக்கு"],
 ("Bharathidasan wrote only about kings.",["He wrote on modern ideas.","He valued women's education."]),
 ["m|Kudumba Vilakku is by|Bharathidasan|Kannadasan|Kamban|Bharathidasan.","m|Renaissance literature is called|மறுமலர்ச்சி|சங்க இலக்கியம்|புராணம்|Maru malarchi.","t|The poet values women's education.|T|Yes.","m|குடும்ப விளக்கு means|lamp of the family|house|book|Lamp of the family.","s|What does பகுத்தறிவு mean?|rationalism;reason|Reasoning.","t|It is a twentieth-century work.|T|Yes."])
T(4,I4,"uyirvagai","Uyirvagai (உயிர்வகை) from Tholkappiyam",
 "Long ago, Tamil scholars sorted living things by how many senses they have.",
 "Uyirvagai classifies living beings by the number of senses: one-sense (ஓரறிவு) beings such as plants feel by touch, two-sense beings add taste, and so on up to six-sense (ஆறறிவு) human beings who have a mind. This classification comes from the Tholkappiyam, the oldest Tamil grammar.",
 "The classification shows that ancient Tamils observed nature carefully. The memorisation poem in the textbook gives this order of beings.",
 "Terms: உயிர்வகை (kinds of life), ஓரறிவு to ஆறறிவு, தொல்காப்பியம் and மனம் (mind).",
 ["உயிர்வகை","ஓரறிவு","ஆறறிவு","தொல்காப்பியம்","மனம்"],
 ("Plants have six senses.",["Plants have one sense.","Humans have six."]),
 ["m|Humans are classed as|ஆறறிவு|ஓரறிவு|ஈரறிவு|Six senses.","m|Plants are classed as|ஓரறிவு|ஆறறிவு|ஐந்தறிவு|One sense.","t|The classification comes from Tholkappiyam.|T|Yes.","m|Tholkappiyam is the oldest|Tamil grammar|Tamil epic|Tamil film|Oldest grammar.","s|What does the sixth sense (arivu) add?|mind;manam;மனம்|The mind.","t|It classes living things by their senses.|T|Yes."])
T(4,I4,"veettirkor-puthagasalai","Veettirkor Puthagasalai (வீட்டிற்கோர் புத்தகசாலை)",
 "A home library makes a home richer than gold.",
 "This lesson opens with Abraham Lincoln's saying that the best friend is the one who brings a good book you have not yet read. It notes that what separates humans from animals is not laughter alone but thinking, and that books spur thinking.",
 "The lesson urges every household to keep a small library and build the habit of reading.",
 "Terms: புத்தகசாலை (library), வாசிப்பு (reading), நூல் (book) and சிந்தனை (thought).",
 ["புத்தகசாலை","வாசிப்பு","நூல்","சிந்தனை","நண்பன்"],
 ("A book is useless without a library building.",["Every home can have a library.","Reading builds thought."]),
 ["m|Who is quoted in the lesson?|Abraham Lincoln|Gandhi|Nehru|Lincoln.","m|The lesson recommends|a library in every home|a sports club|a cinema|Home library.","t|Books spur thinking.|T|Yes.","m|வாசிப்பு means|reading|writing|singing|Reading.","s|What does நூல் mean?|book|A book.","t|Thinking separates humans from animals, says the lesson.|T|Yes."])
T(4,I4,"thunaivinaigal","Grammar: Auxiliary verbs (துணைவினைகள்)",
 "Small helper verbs add shades of meaning to the main verb.",
 "A துணைவினை is a verb that joins the main verb to add a meaning such as completion, continuity or ability. In 'he has eaten', the helper shows that the action is finished.",
 "Common துணைவினைகள் include விடு, கொள், போ, வா, இரு, கொண்டிரு and முடி. They change only the shade of the meaning, and the main verb carries the main idea.",
 "Practise finding the main verb and the helper in sentences. Remember that helper verbs lose their own full meaning when they help.",
 ["துணைவினை","முதன்மை வினை","விடு","கொள்","இரு"],
 ("A helper verb carries the main idea.",["The main verb carries the idea.","The helper adds a shade."]),
 ["m|துணைவினை means|auxiliary verb|noun|adjective|Helper verb.","m|A helper verb adds|a shade of meaning|a new noun|a number|Completion, continuity and so on.","t|The main verb carries the main idea.|T|Yes.","m|Which is a helper verb?|விடு|மரம்|பூ|Vidu.","s|What is a helper verb called?|துணைவினை;thunaivinai|துணைவினை.","t|Helper verbs lose their full meaning.|T|Yes."])
I5="Iyal 5: Arts, Beauty and Newness (கலை, அழகியல், புதுமை)"
T(5,I5,"silpakkalai","Silpakkalai (சிற்பக்கலை) — sculpture",
 "Stone and metal can hold feelings and history.",
 "This lesson says that humans, who first made tools from stone and metal, began to carve sculptures, which marks the beginning of civilisation. Tamils carved their feelings and events in lifeless stone and metal.",
 "The sculptures remain records of history today and show Tamil artistic skill. The lesson invites us to value and protect them.",
 "Terms: சிற்பம் (sculpture), கலை (art), நாகரிகம் (civilisation) and உலோகம் (metal).",
 ["சிற்பம்","கலை","நாகரிகம்","உலோகம்","கல்"],
 ("Sculptures are only for decoration.",["They record history.","They show feelings."]),
 ["m|Sculptures are carved in|stone and metal|paper|water|Stone and metals.","m|சிற்பம் means|sculpture|poem|festival|Sculpture.","t|Sculpture marks early civilisation.|T|Yes.","m|Sculptures serve as|records of history|food|clothes|They preserve history.","s|What does கலை mean?|art|Art.","t|Tamils carved their feelings in stone.|T|Yes."])
T(5,I5,"ravana-kaviyam","Ravana Kaviyam (இராவண காவியம்) by Pulavar Kuzhandhai",
 "A garden of green trees, rivers and birds opens this poem.",
 "Ravana Kaviyam, by Pulavar Kuzhandhai, is a modern epic that tells the Ramayana story from the side of Ravana. The textbook poem opens with a vivid description of a garden full of flowers, trees, river banks, deer, peacocks, cuckoos and parrots.",
 "The poem shows how a poet's words paint nature and how a reader can enjoy the beauty of language. It is one of the memorisation poems.",
 "Terms: காவியம் (epic), இயற்கை வருணனை (nature description), புலவர் குழந்தை and மனப்பாடம்.",
 ["காவியம்","இயற்கை வருணனை","புலவர் குழந்தை","பூஞ்சோலை","மனப்பாடம்"],
 ("Ravana Kaviyam is a story of a Pandya king.",["It retells the Ramayana from Ravana's side.","It is by Pulavar Kuzhandhai."]),
 ["m|Ravana Kaviyam is by|Pulavar Kuzhandhai|Kamban|Valluvar|Pulavar Kuzhandhai.","m|The poem opens with|a garden description|a battle|a feast|Natural beauty.","t|It is a modern epic.|T|Yes.","m|காவியம் means|epic|song|story book|Epic.","s|What does பூஞ்சோலை mean?|flower garden;garden|A garden of flowers.","t|Birds like peacocks and cuckoos are mentioned.|T|Yes."])
T(5,I5,"kalai-pala-valarththal","Kalai Pala Valarththal Eythi (கலை பல வளர்த்தல் எய்தி)",
 "A lawyer is stirred by a musician's playing late at night.",
 "This is a short-story piece in the arts unit. In the textbook extract a lawyer hears music being played again and again, five or six times, ending as if the sound melted into silence. The story shows how an artist's devotion to his art fills the listener.",
 "The unit's message is that art, music and learning should be developed, and that a true artist loves his art above all.",
 "Terms: கலை (art), இசை (music), கீர்த்தனை (a devotional song) and கலைஞன் (artist). Read the full story in your textbook for the details of the plot.",
 ["கலை","இசை","கீர்த்தனை","கலைஞன்","சிறுகதை"],
 ("The lawyer disliked the music.",["He was deeply moved.","The artist played again and again."]),
 ["m|The musician plays the same song|five or six times|once|never|As in the extract.","m|கலைஞன் means|artist|farmer|judge|Artist.","t|The music faded into silence.|T|Yes.","m|கீர்த்தனை is a|devotional song|story|law|Song.","s|What does இசை mean?|music|Music.","t|The piece is about devotion to art.|T|Yes."])
T(5,I5,"vallinam-migum-idangal","Grammar: Where the hard consonant doubles (வல்லினம் மிகும் இடங்கள்)",
 "Sometimes a hard consonant doubles when two words join, as when 'the bird' + 'song' becomes 'bird-song' with an extra sound.",
 "In Tamil, when a word ends in certain sounds, the next word's first hard consonant (க, ச, த, ப) doubles. This is called வல்லினம் மிகுதல். It occurs after words such as அந்த, இந்த, எந்த and after certain suffixes.",
 "For example அந்த + பையன் becomes அந்தப் பையன், and the second case ending ஐ is followed by a doubled consonant, as in மரத்தைப் பார். Also with போன்ற words like இரண்டாம் வேற்றுமை.",
 "Memorise the rules with examples and practise writing sentences. The textbook gives such places as: after அ, இ, உ-type demonstrative words, after the accusative ஐ and after verbal participles ending in ஆ.",
 ["வல்லினம் மிகுதல்","வேற்றுமை","சுட்டு","எழுத்து","புணர்ச்சி"],
 ("The hard consonant never doubles.",["It doubles in some places.","The rules are fixed."]),
 ["m|அந்த + பையன் =|அந்தப் பையன்|அந்தபையன்|அந்தப்பையன்ன்|The hard consonant doubles.","m|வல்லினம் மிகுதல் means|the hard consonant doubles|a word disappears|a vowel changes|By definition.","t|After the case ending ஐ the hard consonant doubles.|T|Yes.","m|Which is a hard consonant?|ப|ம|ர|Vallinam includes க ச ட த ப ற.","s|What is புணர்ச்சி in English?|joining;sandhi|Joining of words.","t|It occurs in specific places.|T|Yes."])
T(5,I5,"thirukkural-iyal5","Thirukkural (திருக்குறள்) — selected couplets, Iyal 5",
 "The shortest verse form carries the biggest ideas.",
 "Thirukkural is a two-line couplet form (kural venba) in which Thiruvalluvar speaks on virtue, wealth and love. The textbook gives selected couplets in this iyal, linked to the theme of arts and beauty.",
 "Each kural is brief but has deep meaning. We should learn its words, its meaning and a daily-life example.",
 "Revise the three parts: அறத்துப்பால், பொருட்பால், காமத்துப்பால் (இன்பத்துப்பால்). Learn how each chapter has ten kurals.",
 ["குறள்","அறத்துப்பால்","பொருட்பால்","இன்பத்துப்பால்","அதிகாரம்"],
 ("Each chapter has twenty kurals.",["Each chapter has ten.","133 chapters make 1330 kurals."]),
 ["m|Kurals per chapter|10|20|5|Ten kurals each.","m|The three parts are aram, porul and|inbam|veeram|kalvi|Inbam.","t|Thirukkural is in kural venba form.|T|Yes.","m|A kural has how many lines?|Two|Four|Six|Two lines.","s|Who wrote the Thirukkural?|Thiruvalluvar;Valluvar|Thiruvalluvar.","t|It is a book of ethics.|T|Yes."])
I6="Iyal 6: Country, Society and Governance (நாடு, சமூகம், அரசு நிருவாகம்)"
T(6,I6,"ina-tamilar-pangu","Indhiya Thesiya Raanuvaththil Thamizhar Pangu (இந்திய தேசிய இராணுவத்தில் தமிழர் பங்கு)",
 "Tamils stood shoulder to shoulder with Netaji in the fight for freedom.",
 "The Indian National Army (INA) was formed for India's freedom, and Tamils were its pillars. The lesson by Ma. Su. Annamalai describes the role of Tamils who fought alongside Netaji Subhas Chandra Bose in the INA and kept the freedom struggle's light burning.",
 "It shows that the fight for freedom included people from all regions and that sacrifice for the nation matters.",
 "Terms: இந்திய தேசிய இராணுவம் (INA), விடுதலைப் போராட்டம் (freedom struggle), நேதாஜி and தியாகம் (sacrifice).",
 ["இந்திய தேசிய இராணுவம்","நேதாஜி","விடுதலைப் போராட்டம்","தியாகம்","தமிழர்"],
 ("The INA had no Tamil members.",["Tamils were its pillars.","They fought with Netaji."]),
 ["m|INA stands for|Indian National Army|Indian Naval Academy|Indian National Alliance|Indian National Army.","m|Tamils fought with|Netaji Subhas Chandra Bose|Tipu Sultan|Ashoka|Netaji.","t|The INA was formed for freedom.|T|Yes.","m|தியாகம் means|sacrifice|sleep|travel|Sacrifice.","s|What does விடுதலை mean?|freedom|Freedom.","t|The lesson praises Tamil sacrifice.|T|Yes."])
T(6,I6,"seevaka-chinthamani","Seevaka Chinthamani (சீவக சிந்தாமணி) by Thiruthakka Thevar",
 "A hero's whole life is told as an epic.",
 "Seevaka Chinthamani is one of the five great Tamil epics, composed by Thiruthakka Thevar. Sangam literature gave lyrical poems; later, epics arose that sing the life of a peerless hero. This epic has Seevakan as its hero.",
 "The epic is known for its beautiful language and is called a 'gem of the Tamil language'. It is among the memorisation poems.",
 "Terms: சீவகன் (the hero), காப்பியம், திருத்தக்கதேவர் and ஐம்பெருங்காப்பியம்.",
 ["சீவகன்","காப்பியம்","திருத்தக்கதேவர்","ஐம்பெருங்காப்பியம்","சிந்தாமணி"],
 ("The hero of the epic is Kovalan.",["The hero is Seevakan.","It is by Thiruthakka Thevar."]),
 ["m|Seevaka Chinthamani is by|Thiruthakka Thevar|Sekkizhar|Ilango|Thiruthakka Thevar.","m|The hero is|Seevakan|Kovalan|Rama|Seevakan.","t|It is one of the five great epics.|T|Yes.","m|சிந்தாமணி means|a wish-giving gem|a sword|a lake|Gem.","s|How many great Tamil epics are there?|five;5|Five.","t|Epics sing the life of a hero.|T|Yes."])
T(6,I6,"vaazhiya-nilane","Vaazhiya Nilane (வாழிய நிலனே) — a poem on the land",
 "A poet wishes long life to the land and its people.",
 "This poem in the unit on the country and society praises the land (நிலம்) and wishes it to flourish. It follows the Sangam habit of blessing a good king and his country with the wish that the land may live long.",
 "The poem links the prosperity of a nation to the goodness of its rulers and people. Read the poem from the textbook and learn its meaning.",
 "Terms: நிலம் (land), வாழ்த்து (blessing), அரசு (government) and நாடு (country). The exact lines are best learnt from your textbook.",
 ["நிலம்","வாழ்த்து","நாடு","அரசு","சங்க இலக்கியம்"],
 ("Vaazhiya Nilane is a prose lesson.",["It is a poem.","It blesses the land."]),
 ["m|Vaazhiya Nilane is|a poem|a play|a story|A poem blessing the land.","m|நிலம் means|land|sea|sky|Land.","t|The poem wishes the land to flourish.|T|Yes.","m|வாழ்த்து means|blessing|curse|journey|Blessing.","s|What does நாடு mean?|country|Country.","t|Good rulers make a country prosper.|T|Yes."])
T(6,I6,"vinnaiyum-saaduvom","Vinnaiyum Saaduvom (விண்ணையும் சாடுவோம்) — Let us leap even into space",
 "A butterfly's wing can stir the weather far away; what can a satellite do?",
 "The lesson begins with the idea that a butterfly's wing flap can have an effect elsewhere in the world. It then explains how satellites launched by India's space department have brought remarkable improvements to people's lives.",
 "It describes India's progress in space and inspires students to reach for science. Satellites help in communication, weather forecasting and mapping.",
 "Terms: விண்வெளி (space), செயற்கைக்கோள் (satellite), இஸ்ரோ (ISRO) and அறிவியல் (science).",
 ["விண்வெளி","செயற்கைக்கோள்","இஸ்ரோ","அறிவியல்","முன்னேற்றம்"],
 ("Satellites do nothing for common people.",["They improve life.","They help weather and communication."]),
 ["m|செயற்கைக்கோள் means|satellite|rocket|planet|Artificial satellite.","m|Satellites help with|communication and weather|only cooking|only sports|Many uses.","t|India has a space programme.|T|Yes.","m|விண்வெளி means|space|sea|forest|Outer space.","s|What does அறிவியல் mean?|science|Science.","t|The lesson inspires students.|T|Yes."])
T(6,I6,"vallinam-miga-idangal","Grammar: Where the hard consonant does not double (வல்லினம் மிகா இடங்கள்)",
 "Not every joining doubles the hard consonant; learn the exceptions.",
 "வல்லினம் மிகா இடங்கள் are the places where the hard consonant does not double when words join. For example, in a vocative or an exclamation, in a verb followed by a noun, and when a word ends in a specific form, no doubling occurs.",
 "Typical cases include the first-case noun followed by its verb (as in 'the bird sang' with no double), words in a series, and sentences with a vocative like 'Come, Kumar'.",
 "Practise with pairs of sentences: one where the consonant doubles and one where it does not. Learn why the meaning changes.",
 ["வல்லினம் மிகாமை","எழுவாய்","விளி","வினை","தொடர்"],
 ("The consonant doubles everywhere.",["There are exceptions.","Vocatives do not double."]),
 ["m|In a vocative the consonant|does not double|always doubles|vanishes|It does not double.","m|The opposite of vallinam migum is|vallinam miga|vallinam theiyum|none|Vallinam miga idangal.","t|There are fixed rules.|T|Yes.","m|A series of nouns generally|does not double|doubles always|has no hard letters|Words in a list do not double.","s|What is விளி?|vocative|Calling case.","t|Learning both rules prevents spelling mistakes.|T|Yes."])
I7="Iyal 7: Virtue, Philosophy and Thought (அறம், தத்துவம், சிந்தனை)"
T(7,I7,"periyarin-sinthanaigal","Periyarin Sinthanaigal (பெரியாரின் சிந்தனைகள்)",
 "A society needs people free of discrimination and full of reason.",
 "This prose lesson says that a society becomes strong when its people are free from discrimination and have a firm mind, and reason (பகுத்தறிவு) is essential to create such people. It presents Periyar, who worked to bring out the people of Tamil Nadu from the darkness of discrimination through the light of reason.",
 "Periyar saw rationalism and self-respect (சுயமரியாதை) as the two eyes of the people. His ideas urge equality and education.",
 "Terms: பகுத்தறிவு (reason), சுயமரியாதை (self-respect), சமூகம் (society) and சிந்தனை (thought).",
 ["பகுத்தறிவு","சுயமரியாதை","சமூகம்","சிந்தனை","சமத்துவம்"],
 ("Periyar opposed education.",["He urged reason and equality.","He spoke of self-respect."]),
 ["m|Periyar stressed|reason and self-respect|war|trade|Pakuththarivu.","m|பகுத்தறிவு means|rational thinking|belief|festival|Reason.","t|Periyar wanted a society free of discrimination.|T|Yes.","m|சுயமரியாதை means|self-respect|pride|anger|Self-respect.","s|What does சமூகம் mean?|society|Society.","t|The lesson calls reason and self-respect two eyes.|T|Yes."])
T(7,I7,"o-en-samakala-thozharkale","O, En Samakala Thozharkale! (ஓ, என் சமகாலத் தோழர்களே!)",
 "A poet speaks directly to the people of his own time.",
 "This poem is addressed to the poet's contemporaries (சமகாலத் தோழர்கள்). It calls them to think, act and build a better world together. It is a memorisation poem in the book.",
 "The poem uses a direct, forceful voice that urges people to change and not to wait.",
 "Terms: சமகாலம் (the present age), தோழர் (comrade), கவிதை (poem) and மனப்பாடம். Read the poem in your textbook for its exact lines.",
 ["சமகாலம்","தோழர்","கவிதை","அழைப்பு","மனப்பாடம்"],
 ("The poem is addressed to kings of the past.",["It addresses contemporaries.","It calls for action."]),
 ["m|The poem addresses|contemporaries|ancestors|animals|My contemporary comrades.","m|தோழர் means|comrade|enemy|king|Friend or comrade.","t|It is a memorisation poem.|T|Yes.","m|சமகாலம் means|the present age|past age|future|Contemporary time.","s|What does கவிதை mean?|poem|A poem.","t|It urges action.|T|Yes."])
T(7,I7,"yasodhara-kaviyam","Yasodhara Kaviyam (யசோதர காவியம்)",
 "Some literature is not only for enjoyment but also teaches how to live.",
 "Yasodhara Kaviyam is one of the five minor Tamil epics (ஐஞ்சிறுகாப்பியங்கள்). The lesson says that literature does not only delight but also teaches ways of life, beginning with Thirukkural and many works on virtue.",
 "It teaches non-violence and compassion towards all living beings, as taught in Jain tradition. It is among the memorisation poems.",
 "Terms: ஐஞ்சிறுகாப்பியம் (five minor epics), அறம் (virtue), அகிம்சை (non-violence) and காவியம்.",
 ["ஐஞ்சிறுகாப்பியம்","அறம்","அகிம்சை","காவியம்","யசோதரன்"],
 ("It is one of the five great epics.",["It is one of the five minor epics.","It teaches non-violence."]),
 ["m|Yasodhara Kaviyam is one of the|five minor epics|five great epics|Sangam books|Aim siru kaappiyam.","m|It teaches|non-violence|war|trade|Compassion.","t|Literature can teach how to live.|T|Yes.","m|அறம் means|virtue|sin|weather|Virtue.","s|What does அகிம்சை mean?|non-violence|Non-violence.","t|It is a memorisation poem.|T|Yes."])
T(7,I7,"makanukku-ezhuthiya-kaditham","Makanukku Ezhuthiya Kaditham (மகனுக்கு எழுதிய கடிதம்) by Na. Muthukumar",
 "A father writes to his son about the world he is growing into.",
 "This is a letter in modern Tamil by Na. Muthukumar. The lesson begins by recalling how people sent messages from smoke and sound signals to letters and now to e-mail, and shows that the form of communication keeps changing.",
 "The letter shows a father's thoughts and advice for his son, and how letters carry feelings. It encourages the habit of writing letters.",
 "Learn the parts of a letter: address, date, salutation, body, closing and signature. Terms: கடிதம் (letter), மின்னஞ்சல் (e-mail) and அஞ்சல் (post).",
 ["கடிதம்","மின்னஞ்சல்","அஞ்சல்","முகவரி","வாழ்த்து"],
 ("Letters are no longer useful.",["Letters carry feelings.","The form changes with time."]),
 ["m|கடிதம் means|letter|poem|book|Letter.","m|மின்னஞ்சல் means|e-mail|post box|phone|Electronic mail.","t|The form of messages has changed over time.|T|Yes.","m|The letter is written to|a son|a king|a teacher|Makanukku.","s|Who wrote the letter?|Na. Muthukumar;Muthukumar|Na. Muthukumar.","t|A letter has a salutation and a closing.|T|Yes."])
T(7,I7,"yappilakkanam","Grammar: Prosody (யாப்பிலக்கணம்)",
 "Poetry has a hidden skeleton of letters, syllables and feet.",
 "யாப்பிலக்கணம் is the grammar of verse. Its parts are எழுத்து, அசை (syllable unit), சீர் (foot), தளை (linking), அடி (line), தொடை (rhyme) and பா (verse type). Asai is of two kinds, நேரசை and நிரையசை.",
 "Words made of asai form a சீர்; sīrs form an அடி; and lines form a பா such as வெண்பா, ஆசிரியப்பா, வஞ்சிப்பா or கலிப்பா. Thirukkural is written in kural venba.",
 "Practise splitting a line into asai and naming the சீர். Learn the terms அசை, சீர், தளை, அடி, தொடை and பா.",
 ["யாப்பு","அசை","சீர்","தளை","தொடை"],
 ("Prosody is the grammar of prose.",["It is the grammar of verse.","It has asai, seer and adi."]),
 ["m|Yappu is the grammar of|verse|prose|numbers|Verse.","m|Asai is of two kinds: nerasai and|nirayasai|vallasai|melasai|Niraiyasai.","t|Seers join to form an adi.|T|Yes.","m|Thirukkural is in|kural venba|asiriyappa|kali|Kural venba.","s|What is a line of verse called?|அடி;adi|An adi.","t|Thodai means rhyme.|T|Yes."])
T(7,I7,"thirukkural-iyal7","Thirukkural (திருக்குறள்) — selected couplets, Iyal 7",
 "Virtue and thought are the heart of Thirukkural.",
 "This selection of kurals from Thirukkural speaks of virtue (அறம்) and thoughtful living. Thiruvalluvar says that a good life is built on goodness of mind.",
 "The kurals are short, and each can guide our actions. Learn them with their meanings and use them in daily life.",
 "Revise the chapter names, the meaning of each word, and the message. Remember that there are 1330 kurals in 133 chapters.",
 ["குறள்","அறம்","மனம்","வாழ்க்கை","அதிகாரம்"],
 ("Thirukkural speaks only of love.",["It speaks of virtue, wealth and love.","This selection is on virtue."]),
 ["m|Thirukkural speaks of|virtue, wealth and love|only war|only food|Three parts.","m|Total kurals|1330|133|1000|1330.","t|Each kural has two lines.|T|Yes.","m|அறம் means|virtue|wealth|love|Virtue.","s|Who is the author?|Thiruvalluvar;Valluvar|Thiruvalluvar.","t|Thirukkural helps shape conduct.|T|Yes."])
